<title>CANADA: CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</title>
<headline>CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vacant space in Canadian Prairie primary elevators increased to 35 percent in the week ended June 2 while railcar unloads exceeded targets, the Canadian Wheat Board said.</p>
<p>The average vacancy in Prairie elevators was 35 percent, up from 32 percent on May 25, it said.</p>
<p>Manitoba showed the most space available at 42 percent followed by Alberta at 34 percent and Saskatchewan at 33 percent.</p>
<p>Vancouver unloaded 3,103 railcars versus the 3,300 target. Prince Rupert unloaded 1,373 railcars versus the 1,300 target.</p>
<p>Thunder Bay unloaded 3,815 railcars versus the 3,075 hopper car target.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
